## Law
- [L1] Dispatch is ticket id + delta + budget declaration, never a re-pasted brief: a re-pasted contract drifts from the ticket and the worker follows the stale copy, which is the misreading that cost the reference fleet a 207K-token compaction. (orchestrator, {date})
- [L1] Workers never move their own ticket file and never write verdicts; evidence lands in state/evidence/<id>/ and the reviewer or orchestrator moves the file: self-acceptance is the failure this fleet exists to prevent, so "I finished, marking it done" is never grounds. (orchestrator, {date})
- [L1] Timestamps are `date -u` verbatim, never local time relabeled: relabeled clocks made incident order unrecoverable in the reference fleet, so a local stamp with a Z pasted on it is worse than no stamp. (orchestrator, {date})

